.LONG TERM...
Issued at 1230 AM PDT Wed Oct 21 2026
(Thursday through Tuesday)

The rain and thunderstorm threat are gone by Friday. With the trough
to our east, building high pressure brings warm and dry conditions
into early next week. Euro and GFS ensemble members suggest warming
to near seasonal averages meanwhile precipitable water values are
forecast to dip below the 25th percentile. Monday onward, there is a
great deal of uncertainty on when the weak ridge breaks down. An
energetic Central Pacific plus the most recent 6-10 day Climate
Prediction Center precipitation outlook suggests another trough
coming our way with the potential for more rain.

