Currently VFR with clouds and rain showers pushing in from the
south. The best chances for thunderstorms are for the Monterey Bay
terminals this afternoon and this evening, 22Z to 02Z. Elsewhere,
rain showers are expected through the TAF period, spreading from
south to north. The best chances for rain showers to occur at a
terminal will be this afternoon and this evening as coverage and
intensity increases; however, chances linger through the TAF period
with wrap around rain showers expected overnight into tomorrow
morning. Winds will be light and diurnal except when rain
shower/thunderstorm driven. Low confidence on sub-VFR ceilings
developing overnight; however, sub-VFR ceilings and visibilities can
be expected briefly if a rain shower passes directly over a
terminal.

Vicinity of SFO...Currently VFR with northwesterly flow. Clouds will
continue to lower through the morning with rain showers expected by
this afternoon. The best chances for rain showers directly at the
terminal today are between 22Z and 04Z with wrap around rain showers
continuing through the end of the TAF period. Conditions may improve
towards the tail end of the TAF period at or after 20Z; however,
another chance of rain showers is expected during this time as
the upper-level low pulls east.

SFO Bridge Approach...Relatively higher chance for thunderstorms;
however, the best chances remain south of SJC. Clouds will lower and
rain showers will occur sooner than SFO. Clouds at or below FL070
are expected through the TAF period; however, conditions may briefly
improve between rain showers.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Currently VFR with southeasterly flow at
both terminals and rain beginning to be observed at MRY. There is a
chance for thunderstorms today with the best chances being between
22Z and 02Z. Rain showers will increase in coverage and intensity
this evening. Wrap around rain showers are expected overnight and
into tomorrow morning, likely less in coverage and intensity. Winds
will be light and diurnal except when rain shower/thunderstorm
driven.

